---

<DocsPage slug="install">
  <h1>Install the lace-app-sdk</h1>
  <p class="lpd-sub">
    The public, versioned contract surface for building apps on LACE. A facade
    over the live platform contracts — never a fork of them.
  </p>

  <div class="lp-code">
    <div class="lp-code-head"><span>terminal</span><em>bash</em></div>
    <pre><code set:html={codeInstall} /></pre>
  </div>

  <h2 id="what-you-get">What the SDK guarantees</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Facade, not fork</strong> — every symbol re-exports live core contracts; the builder and the sidecar resolve to the same code.</li>
    <li><strong>Stability boundary</strong> — apps import only <code class="lp-inline-code">lace_app_sdk</code>; breaking a published symbol is a major version bump with a deprecation window.</li>
    <li><strong>Governed by construction</strong> — data, tools, routes, and agents flow through platform services with tenancy, policy, and audit applied.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2 id="requirements">Requirements</h2>
  <p>
    Python 3.11 or later, and access to a LACE tenant to publish against. The
    SDK itself can be installed and explored without a tenant; publishing an app
    requires one.
  </p>

  <p>
    Next: the <a href="/docs/quickstart">quickstart</a> builds a working
    governed application from four small files.
  </p>
</DocsPage>
